# Stokes linear solve with block preconditioning ([elmer] linear_stokes = "block", or `ess run --linear-stokes block`).
# Every line that is not blank and does not start with # or // goes verbatim into the Stokes solver section of the
# template (in place of the direct / iterative keywords). A STARTING POINT: check it against the block settings you
# use with Elmer/Ice and replace it with those; the keyword set depends on the Elmer version.
# Velocity block (1: the 3 velocity components) and pressure block (2): outer GCR, block Gauss-Seidel, the
# velocity block by an inner Krylov solve, the pressure block (Schur complement) approximated in Elmer.
Linear System Solver = Iterative
Linear System Iterative Method = GCR
Linear System GCR Restart = Integer 200
Linear System Max Iterations = 1000
Linear System Convergence Tolerance = 1.0e-8
Linear System Abort Not Converged = False
Linear System Residual Output = 10
Block Preconditioner = Logical True
Block Gauss-Seidel = Logical True
Block Matrix Reuse = Logical False
Block Structure(4) = Integer 1 1 1 2
Block Order(2) = Integer 1 2
Block 11: Linear System Solver = Iterative
Block 11: Linear System Iterative Method = GCR
Block 11: Linear System GCR Restart = Integer 100
Block 11: Linear System Max Iterations = 500
Block 11: Linear System Convergence Tolerance = 1.0e-4
Block 11: Linear System Preconditioning = ILU0
Block 22: Linear System Solver = Iterative
Block 22: Linear System Iterative Method = GCR
Block 22: Linear System Max Iterations = 200
Block 22: Linear System Convergence Tolerance = 1.0e-4
Block 22: Linear System Preconditioning = Diagonal
